WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:05.379
As Avengers: Endgame careens towards theaters,
the question every fan is asking is who's

00:00:05.379 --> 00:00:08.420
going to put an end to the Mad Titan Thanos.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:14.190
Of all the possibilities, no one makes more
sense than the MCU's first hero - Iron Man.

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:17.180
"Is it better to be feared, or respected?

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:21.280
I say, is it too much to ask for both?"

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:25.840
The Infinity Stones may look pretty, but they've
proven pretty deadly to people who come in

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:30.710
contact with them, even when they aren't combined
together in a big golden glove.

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:35.030
In Thor: The Dark World, Jane Foster gets
her life leeched out of her thanks to a close

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:37.190
encounter with the Reality Stone.

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:41.970
And in Guardians of the Galaxy, Peter Quill
was nearly annihilated by the Power Stone,

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:45.330
until the other guardians stepped up and shared
the burden.

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:50.000
That's partly why Thanos' ease in wielding
the stones is so unsettling; it seems like

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.110
the Mad Titan is just made of stronger stuff.

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:57.620
However, a few humans have also been able
to use the fully-powered Infinity Gauntlet

00:00:57.620 --> 00:00:58.989
in the comics.

00:00:58.989 --> 00:01:02.980
Among those hallowed few is none other than
Tony Stark.

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:07.650
While the MCU has diverged from its comics
roots in more than a few ways, it's not hard

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:13.040
to imagine movie Tony wielding an Infinity
Gauntlet to revive his fallen comrades.

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:17.060
It's fun to play along, sure, but we know
they're coming back one way or another.

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:19.530
You saw the Spider-Man trailer, right?

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:24.030
If the Avengers go through the trouble of
stealing Thanos' gauntlet, or somehow make

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:27.189
their own, who would do the honor of wearing
it?

00:01:27.189 --> 00:01:31.500
It's a pretty expensive piece of jewelry,
so maybe it should be handled by the highest-paid

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:32.740
person in the MCU.

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:35.760
"You can't come empty-handed, you know?

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:38.320
Otherwise I would not be an Iron Gentleman."

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:43.120
Unlike some of the Avengers, Tony Stark is
a self-made superhero.

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:46.030
We're not talking about his inherited wealth,
of course.

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:49.979
What makes Tony so impressive is how he got
himself his powers.

00:01:49.979 --> 00:01:55.380
He didn't become a superhero thanks to science
experiments, a radioactive spider, or a deadbeat

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:56.430
celestial dad.

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:59.509
He just rolled up his sleeves and did it.

00:01:59.509 --> 00:02:03.020
"Tony Stark was able to build this in a cave!

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:06.070
With a box of scraps!"

00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:10.819
The first glimpse we've gotten of Mr. Stark
in Endgame looks pretty dire, but we definitely

00:02:10.819 --> 00:02:14.340
don't think Tony is dying out there in the
vacuum of space.

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:17.999
He's going to puzzle out a way to get back
to Earth, and then put all his resources into

00:02:17.999 --> 00:02:23.180
coming up with a solution, whether it's a
time machine, a thousand new suits, or a good-guy

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:24.470
sequel to Ultron.

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:26.999
"We're mad scientists."

00:02:26.999 --> 00:02:31.560
We've seen Tony's army of backup suits already,
but don't forget that he also built custom

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:34.230
suits for War Machine and Spider-Man.

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:38.879
So what would happen if he built custom suits
or gear for more of the surviving Avengers,

00:02:38.879 --> 00:02:43.090
maybe combining his know-how with some Hank
Pym shrinking tech?

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:47.359
Imagine Captain America with some powerful
Stark-designed armor, making him and his shield

00:02:47.359 --> 00:02:48.410
even stronger.

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:53.469
Actually, you don't need to imagine it, because
it's straight from the comics - as is Pepper

00:02:53.469 --> 00:02:57.730
Potts own' Rescue armor, which we might end
up seeing in the movie.

00:02:57.730 --> 00:03:03.299
Basically, if Iron Man can put up a pretty
good fight one-on-one using just his suit,

00:03:03.299 --> 00:03:07.280
Thanos doesn't stand a chance against a whole
teched-out team of Avengers.

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:11.840
Iron Man might have put up a good fight against
Thanos, but all the tricks in his nanotech

00:03:11.859 --> 00:03:16.309
suit have got nothing on Stormbreaker, Thor's
new ax.

00:03:16.309 --> 00:03:21.339
Forged by the giant dwarf Eitri out of Uru
metal and a dash of Groot, the weapon managed

00:03:21.339 --> 00:03:26.019
to cleave through Thanos' chest when he was
at full power, nearly ending the Infinity

00:03:26.019 --> 00:03:28.719
War while it was still in part one.

00:03:28.719 --> 00:03:34.370
If one Asgardian weapon could do so much damage,
a few more might just finish the job - especially

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:37.499
with Tony Stark collaborating on the design.

00:03:37.499 --> 00:03:41.689
This is another thing that's happened before
in the comics, specifically the event comic

00:03:41.689 --> 00:03:43.339
"Fear Itself."

00:03:43.339 --> 00:03:48.089
In that story, some of Marvel's best and brightest
get their own Asgardian weapons courtesy of

00:03:48.089 --> 00:03:50.629
a Stark-Odin collaboration.

00:03:50.629 --> 00:03:56.329
While the MCU's Odin might be dead, he was
replaced as the High Father by Thor - and

00:03:56.329 --> 00:04:00.559
with great power, there must also come the
responsibility to make radical new weapons

00:04:00.559 --> 00:04:02.749
to kill aliens with.

00:04:02.749 --> 00:04:08.119
If Eitri survived Thanos' decimation, it's
not crazy to imagine the Avengers going back

00:04:08.119 --> 00:04:12.370
to re-arm themselves with technically-enhanced,
godlike weaponry.

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:13.370
Why not?

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:17.129
Hulk couldn't beat Thanos the first time,
but what if he had a sword like Heimdall's?

00:04:17.129 --> 00:04:21.269
"My old man had a philosophy: 'Peace means
having a bigger stick than the other guy.'”

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:23.640
"That's a great line, coming from a guy selling
the sticks."

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:28.720
While Avengers: Endgame's plot details are
still under wraps, rumor has it that the key

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:34.770
to defeating Thanos will heavily involve time
travel - the MCU's version of a cheat code.

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:40.180
Supposedly, the film will feature the surviving
Avengers scrambling across time, intersecting

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:44.930
with set pieces from previous movies, like
the Avengers' Battle of New York.

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:48.860
We don't know if they're recruiting people
from the past, stealing Infinity Stones from

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:53.430
the time stream, or something else, but if
the time travel rumors are true, then the

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:59.139
movie is going to feel almost like a greatest
hits collection of the MCU's first ten years.

00:04:59.139 --> 00:05:04.750
One intriguing possibility time travel raises
is a possible reunion between Tony and his

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:06.580
father, Howard Stark.

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:12.020
It's not as crazy as it seems - if you remember,
Papa Stark helped forge Captain America's

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:14.719
shield, played a vital role in the formation
of the S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:05:14.719 --> 00:05:20.550
organization, and was basically the 1940s
version of his genius playboy son, flaws and

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:21.699
all.

00:05:21.699 --> 00:05:25.639
While Endgame seems packed to the gills with
characters already, it would definitely be

00:05:25.639 --> 00:05:31.009
satisfying for Tony to finally get closure
with his dad - and just maybe, a little family

00:05:31.009 --> 00:05:33.800
insight into how to save the world.

